      "source": [
        "# Everything above answers a fixed set of topics with hand-written, verified\n",
        "# copy. That is the right design for the questions we anticipated: it is\n",
        "# instant, deterministic, and cannot invent a legal fact.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# This section adds the other half -- a genuine language model that handles\n",
        "# questions nobody scripted (\"is this a good buy for a foreigner?\",\n",
        "# \"explain possessory rights like I'm five\"). It follows the Workshop 2\n",
        "# brief: a free Hugging Face model, no API key, no account.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# The two layers are deliberately NOT interchangeable:\n",
        "#\n",
        "#   intent matched   -> scripted answer   (fast, exact, legally checked)\n",
        "#   no intent match  -> LLM answer        (flexible, grounded, hedged)\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Grounding matters here. A 1.5B model asked cold about Thai land law will\n",
        "# confidently invent section numbers and fees. So every request carries the\n",
        "# dataset from TITLES as context, and the system prompt forbids going\n",
        "# beyond it. That turns the model from \"a thing that knows Thai law\" into\n",
        "# \"a thing that explains our verified table in plain language\", which is a\n",
        "# far safer job to give it.\n",
        "\n",
        "LLM_MODEL_ID = \"Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\"\n",
        "LLM_MAX_NEW_TOKENS = 320\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_knowledge_context() -> str:\n",
        "    \"\"\"Compact, factual context block handed to the model on every turn.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Generated from TITLES rather than typed out, so the model can never be\n",
        "    briefed on facts that differ from the CSV or the on-screen tables.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    lines = [\"VERIFIED DATA -- Thai land title deeds (Workshop 2 dataset):\"]\n",
        "    for title in TITLES.values():\n",
        "        marker = \"  [THIS IS THE TITLE THE USER IS ASKING ABOUT]\" if title.key == \"green\" else \"\"\n",
        "        lines.append(f\"\\n{title.color_name} Garuda / {title.short_name} ({title.thai_name}){marker}\")\n",
        "        for field, label in SPEC_FIELDS:\n",
        "            if field == \"thai_name\":\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "            lines.append(f\"  - {label}: {getattr(title, field)}\")\n",
        "    lines.append(\n",
        "        \"\\nAdditional verified points about the Green Garuda (N.S.3K):\"\n",
        "        \"\\n  - Under Section 1375 of the Civil and Commercial Code, continuous\"\n",
        "        \"\\n    occupation for 1 year can support an adverse possession claim\"\n",
        "        \"\\n    (10 years for Red Chanote).\"\n",
        "        \"\\n  - It can be upgraded to Chanote by applying at the Provincial or\"\n",
        "        \"\\n    District Land Office for a ground GPS cadastral survey.\"\n",
        "        \"\\n  - 'Confirmed possessory right' is not ownership: the state holds\"\n",
        "        \"\\n    the underlying title until conversion to Chanote.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "LLM_SYSTEM_PROMPT = f\"\"\"{ADVISOR_PERSONA.strip()}\n",
        "\n",
        "{build_knowledge_context()}\n",
        "\n",
        "RULES YOU MUST FOLLOW:\n",
        "1. Answer ONLY from the verified data above. It is your entire knowledge base.\n",
        "2. If the answer is not in that data, say plainly that you do not have it and\n",
        "   suggest confirming with the local Land Office or a licensed Thai lawyer.\n",
        "   Never invent a fee, a tax rate, a deadline, or a section number.\n",
        "3. Never give a definitive legal ruling on someone's specific situation.\n",
        "   You give general orientation; a licensed Thai lawyer gives advice.\n",
        "4. If the question has nothing to do with Thai land titles, say so briefly\n",
